# MaaS Reference Documentation

See [ADR-0006](docs/adr/0006-maas-documentation-sources.md) for the full decision record on source precedence.

## Authoritative Sources (in priority order)

### 1. Red Hat Official Documentation (PRIMARY)

- **MaaS guide:** https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_openshift_ai_self-managed/3.4/html-single/govern_llm_access_with_models-as-a-service/index
- **RHOAI 3.4 release notes:** https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_openshift_ai_self-managed/3.4/html/release_notes/
- **RHCL / Kuadrant:** https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_connectivity_link/1.1
- **Supported configs:** https://access.redhat.com/articles/rhoai-supported-configs-3.x

Use for: GA/TP status, supported configurations, operator channels, DSC setup, Gateway config.

### 2. Upstream MaaS Documentation (SECONDARY)

- **Docs site:** https://opendatahub-io.github.io/models-as-a-service/latest/
- **GitHub:** https://github.com/opendatahub-io/models-as-a-service

Use for: CRD field reference (MaaSModelRef, MaaSSubscription, MaaSAuthPolicy, ExternalModel, Tenant), controller behavior, auto-created resources, annotations, migration guides, API reference.

### 3. Upstream MaaS Repository (TERTIARY)

- **Source code:** https://github.com/opendatahub-io/models-as-a-service

Use for: resolving doc conflicts, CRD source of truth, PR-based bug fixes, kustomize manifests.

### 4. RHOAI BU Cluster Reference (IMPLEMENTATION PATTERNS)

- **GitOps repo:** https://github.com/rh-aiservices-bu/rhoaibu-cluster

Use for: proven deployment patterns when implementing **new MaaS/RHOAI features** — model serving configs, gateway setup, multi-model layouts, GPU/CPU image choices, observability wiring. Review `components/` and `clusters/` before designing from scratch. Product docs and ADRs still take precedence; this repo is a secondary reference for "how Red Hat BU does it in production."

## When to Consult

- **CRD spec fields** → Upstream docs or repo CRD definitions
- **Is feature X GA?** → Red Hat docs
- **Gateway / Route config** → Red Hat docs, then upstream
- **Auth pipeline (MaaSAuthPolicy)** → Upstream docs (controller behavior)
- **Rate limiting (MaaSSubscription)** → Upstream docs + [ADR-0005](docs/adr/0005-maas-subscription-model.md)
- **Kuadrant (AuthPolicy, RLP, TRLP)** → RHCL docs
- **Bug / unexpected behavior** → Upstream repo issues/PRs
- **Operator channels** → Red Hat docs
- **New feature design / deployment patterns** → [RHOAI BU Cluster](https://github.com/rh-aiservices-bu/rhoaibu-cluster) (secondary reference), then adapt to this repo's module structure

## Validation Rules

1. **Do NOT guess** CRD fields for MaaSModelRef, MaaSSubscription, MaaSAuthPolicy, or Tenant — look them up.
2. **Use `context7` MCP** or `WebFetch` to retrieve current docs when implementing changes.
3. **Cite the source** in ADRs and commit messages.
4. **Conflict resolution**: Red Hat docs win. If upstream has a feature not in Red Hat docs, treat as TP/unsupported.

## Key Components

| Component | CRD / API Group | Purpose |
|-----------|----------------|---------|
| LLMInferenceService | `kserve.io/v1alpha1` | Model serving (KServe + vLLM) |
| MaaSModelRef | `maas.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` | Model reference in /v1/models API |
| MaaSSubscription | `maas.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` | Tier-based token rate limits |
| MaaSAuthPolicy | `maas.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` | API key authentication |
| Tenant | `maas.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` | Telemetry and multi-tenancy |
| Gateway | `gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1` | API gateway (data-science-gateway-class) |
| AuthPolicy | `kuadrant.io/v1` | Kuadrant auth enforcement |
| TokenRateLimitPolicy | `kuadrant.io/v1alpha1` | Token-based rate limiting |
